t for the selected control, before applying the discount exception.","name":"offers_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Every gift component in the assessed offer qualifies as a discount of fees or charges; any non-discount gift component makes this false.","name":"all_gifts_are_fee_discounts","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or (not offers_gift) all_gifts_are_fee_discounts)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_link promotes_authorised_funds)"},"local_id":"r2","questions":["Is the fund setting an application limit of this circular only, with broader obligations established independently by the complete Code?"],"statement":"Read paragraph 10 as applying the referenced gift rule within this circular’s SFC-authorised-fund subject. Distributors should not offer non-discount gifts linked to promoting a specific such fund or a particular fund type, including funds grouped by fund house. The retained text leaves application to other investment products for determination from the complete Code and FAQ.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control within the circular’s fund context"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.48c1efcdf253e1612cde1651","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"555b5e195340bc01e00206c1710938e0825bc0ce647e5b64e549865000b8908c","candidate_id":"candidate.b156638fa54d43848fae18e328bf51bf","commitment":"265f351a2fec57605a484f647c0d9bcbfdc50dd2fd7aad34e736c613fbc76940","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.265f351a2fec57605a484f64","order":2,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["Assess one identified benefit offered by one actor in one promotion to one client; assess distinct benefits separately.","The actor is assessed using u1’s distributor definition. Coverage of persons who do not distribute SFC-authorised funds is unresolved.","A qualifying discount excludes that benefit only. A separate non-discount gift in the same promotion remains independently assessable.","Actual investor distraction is the stated rationale, not an additional factual prerequisite.","The formalization is a conditional reading of the retained standard; it does not establish temporal applicability or resolve missing authorities."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement as investors may be distracted from the unique features and risks of such particular funds3.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"2 The Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"u29"}],"distinction":"R1 gives operative weight to u14’s generic investment-product wording. For a distributor within u1, an otherwise qualifying gift linked to a non-fund investment product is within this selected reading. R2 excludes that case from its scope. The strongest uncertainty is whether the circular is restating the Code’s general reach or only describing its fund-specific application.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary that distributes SFC-authorised funds, within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion concerns an SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of SFC-authorised fund.","name":"is_authorised_fund_promotion","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u14","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The actor offers the identified benefit to a client in the assessed promotion; delivery or acceptance is not required.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift for the selected paragraph 3.11 control, before applying the discount exception; an incentive or guaranteed return does not establish this automatically.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The benefit is offered in promoting a specific investment product or a particular investment-product type, including a type connection established by how the benefit is offered; examples include certain fund types or funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14","u30"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_offered_to_client benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount) has_product_promotion_connection)","result_type":"bool","scope":"is_distributor"},"local_id":"gift_scope_r1","questions":["Does u14’s generic investment-product wording govern promotions beyond SFC-authorised funds by a distributor defined in u1?","How does the full Code determine actor coverage beyond the circular’s distributor definition?"],"statement":"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-offer restriction, general-product reading. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, if the intermediary offers a client a benefit that qualifies as a gift, the benefit is not a discount of fees or charges, and its offer promotes a specific investment product or a particular investment-product type, the offer departs from the stated should-not-offer standard. A product-type connection includes the specified fund-category and fund-house connections. Structured-product status and proof of actual distraction are not prerequisites. Within scope, a true formal result flags that departure; a false result addresses only this selected benefit and control.","subject":"Paragraph-10 gift-promotion control"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.265f351a2fec57605a484f64","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"1ced75d370b194c115b20946d8343dc198fe2b60cc3c4806e8a4b533cf409e58","candidate_id":"candidate.f45b3171601e4e4baf6279e9909ccfbc","commitment":"6c0256c9bafa62f9e72fe4e8ffce826e6ac0639235f5df2bb4381e80fa78d58f","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.6c0256c9bafa62f9e72fe4e8","order":3,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["Assess one identified benefit offered by one actor in one promotion to one client; assess distinct benefits separately.","Read the generic wording in u14 within the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","A qualifying discount excludes that benefit only. A separate non-discount gift in the same promotion remains independently assessable.","Actual investor distraction is the stated rationale, not an additional factual prerequisite.","The formalization is a conditional reading of the retained standard; it does not establish temporal applicability or resolve missing authorities."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO, distributors are reminded to have regard to paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct provides that distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns","unit_id":"u15"},{"quote":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"}],"distinction":"R2 limits the application established by this circular to SFC-authorised fund promotions, while retaining every operative gift condition and the discount exception. A promotion of another investment product falls outside this selected formal scope, without implying permission under the Code. Its strongest weakness is u14’s unqualified reference to investment products rather than only funds.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed actor is an intermediary that distributes SFC-authorised funds, within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion concerns an SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of SFC-authorised fund.","name":"is_authorised_fund_promotion","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u14","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The actor offers the identified benefit to a client in the assessed promotion; delivery or acceptance is not required.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift for the selected paragraph 3.11 control, before applying the discount exception; an incentive or guaranteed return does not establish this automatically.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The benefit is offered in promoting a specific investment product or a particular investment-product type, including a type connection established by how the benefit is offered; examples include certain fund types or funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14","u30"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_offered_to_client benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount) has_product_promotion_connection)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor is_authorised_fund_promotion)"},"local_id":"gift_scope_r2","questions":["Does the fund-focused context limit the application stated here despite u14’s generic wording?","Does the referenced FAQ clarify whether a broad fund-platform promotion has the required product-type connection?"],"statement":"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-offer restriction, fund-context reading. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, assess this restriction when the promotion concerns an SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such fund. If the intermediary offers a client a gift, the gift is not a discount of fees or charges, and its offer has the specified product or product-type promotional connection, the offer departs from the stated should-not-offer standard. Fund-house groupings can supply that connection. Structured-product status and proof of actual distraction are not prerequisites. Within scope, a true formal result flags that departure; other products are outside this reading’s selected scope, with their treatment under the full Code unresolved.","subject":"Paragraph-10 gift-promotion control"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.6c0256c9bafa62f9e72fe4e8","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"15472d3c01402a98a3fa2a609448678225c2640c4549fe2d091e8127ee6aa7e1","candidate_id":"candidate.6f187120d7854e10984f192768f02b1c","commitment":"e161e5517b4d4cbf89c7546ba9fc7c6cb3a1ccd55ecfa0db6ec02b1f3e42b8a7","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.e161e5517b4d4cbf89c7546b","order":4,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The selected control is assessed for one identified benefit offer by a distributor to a client in the SFC-authorised-fund setting.","A direct promotional nexus may arise from express promotion or eligibility terms; it need not require a completed investment.","Gift and discount classifications are supplied judgments, not inferred merely from the label 'additional return'.","The result means the offer is flagged by this selected gift-control reading; it is not a determination of legal liability or overall compliance."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"}],"distinction":"Requires a direct promotional nexus. Consider an account-opening gift available regardless of investment choice, presented prominently alongside a campaign devoted to funds from one fund house, but with no express statement or eligibility term connecting the gift to those funds. If the presentation creates a contextual association but no direct nexus, this reading does not flag it; R2 does. Mere proximity without a meaningful association satisfies neither reading.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed offer is by an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds to a client in that distribution setting.","name":"distributor_client_setting","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered to the client and qualifies as a gift for the selected paragraph 3.11 control.","name":"gift_offered","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception.","name":"fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer expressly promotes, or its eligibility terms directly connect it to, a specific investment product or a particular product type, including funds from a particular fund house.","name":"direct_product_nexus","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The manner or campaign context of offering the gift meaningfully associates it with a specific investment product or particular product type, independently of an express promotion or eligibility connection.","name":"contextual_product_nexus","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and gift_offered (not fee_discount) direct_product_nexus)","result_type":"bool","scope":"distributor_client_setting"},"local_id":"gift_direct_nexus","questions":["Does 'linked' require the direct nexus proposed here? The final sentence of u14 may instead deliberately reach indirect promotional associations."],"statement":"Read 'in promoting' as requiring a direct connection between the gift offer and promotion of a specified product or product type. The final sentence prevents avoidance through promotion of a fund category or fund house instead of a named fund, while retaining that direct connection. A qualifying fee discount remains excepted.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: direct product connection"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.e161e5517b4d4cbf89c7546b","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"1ec8bb5b62e8a4e2d2102a4deb5f614765043e712875cc812e04515fa91746c2","candidate_id":"candidate.b3c06ea9589e47d0b1888ebeb56c28fb","commitment":"216d0d11256996f75bf93a48b87d888660687d4785d1b47d2a758f8bc21afc50","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.216d0d11256996f75bf93a48","order":5,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The selected control is assessed for one identified benefit offer by a distributor to a client in the SFC-authorised-fund setting.","A meaningful product association created by the manner of offering can suffice without product-specific gift eligibility.","Actual investor distraction is not a separate factual prerequisite; the stated purpose informs the linkage interpretation.","Gift and discount classifications are supplied judgments. The result flags only this selected control."],"citations":[{"quote":"The purpose of the requirement is to avoid the use of gifts to distract investors from the features and risks of a particular product.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"other than a discount of fees or charges","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"}],"distinction":"Reaches a meaningful association produced by campaign presentation as well as an express connection. In the account-opening-gift example in R1, contextual linkage to one fund house flags the non-discount gift even though eligibility is investment-neutral. This reading has stronger support in 'offered in such a way' and the distraction rationale, but the missing FAQ prevents settling how much contextual association suffices.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed offer is by an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds to a client in that distribution setting.","name":"distributor_client_setting","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u14","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit is offered to the client and qualifies as a gift for the selected paragraph 3.11 control.","name":"gift_offered","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The assessed benefit qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within the stated exception.","name":"fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer expressly promotes, or its eligibility terms directly connect it to, a specific investment product or a particular product type, including funds from a particular fund house.","name":"direct_product_nexus","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The manner or campaign context of offering the gift meaningfully associates it with a specific investment product or particular product type, independently of an express promotion or eligibility connection.","name":"contextual_product_nexus","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and gift_offered (not fee_discount) (or direct_product_nexus contextual_product_nexus))","result_type":"bool","scope":"distributor_client_setting"},"local_id":"gift_contextual_nexus","questions":["What distinguishes a meaningful contextual product association from incidental placement alongside fund advertising under the missing FAQ?"],"statement":"Read 'offered in such a way that they are linked' as extending the control to indirect but meaningful promotional associations created by presentation or campaign design. A non-discount gift linked in that manner to a product or fund-house category falls within the selected control even when its eligibility terms are product-neutral. The fee-discount exception continues to apply.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: contextual product connection"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.216d0d11256996f75bf93a48","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"d6eee4d001f89edd7e3a7f13961ab020797856ca2680c6db3814c3ff33307a35","candidate_id":"candidate.4e9928d5afdf4c6d811ed93b6b3e09f5","commitment":"11ff0fa005c13e8c070d1aac9a9b5f73b63d2cbec90ad880c992f50ecf1b9773","depth":1,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.11ff0fa005c13e8c070d1aac","order":6,"parent":"node.84e49f3d524cb308835f7db4","reading":{"assumptions":["Assess one identified offer or proposed offer to a client.","The circular’s distributor category supplies actor scope; u14 supplies broader investment-product scope.","The discount exception applies to both specific-product and product-type promotions.","For the offer-level screen, each gift component is assessed separately; any non-discount gift prevents a pass.","A true result is a selected paragraph-10 gift-control pass only when scope is true. It establishes neither overall compliance nor legal correctness.","Unknown facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"Even where the guaranteed returns offered would not constitute a “structured product” under the SFO","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"unless the SFC has authorised the issue or an exemption applies.","unit_id":"u10"}],"distinction":"Retains the parent’s broader product scope and the discount exception throughout u14. The exception-attachment investigation does not support removing the exception for product-type-linked gifts or importing section 103 exemptions into this control. In the supplied probe, this reading has true scope and a true selected result; the unknown fund-promotion fact is irrelevant here. The strongest uncertainty is the broader scope without the complete Code provision.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the circular’s distributor category.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed activity promotes a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to a client, including a substantively linked gift arrangement of the kind described in u14.","name":"has_product_promotion_link","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed promotion concerns SFC-authorised funds.","name":"promotes_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed offer includes a benefit classified as a gift for the selected control, before applying the discount exception.","name":"offers_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Every gift component in the assessed offer qualifies as a discount of fees or charges; any non-discount gift component makes this false.","name":"all_gifts_are_fee_discounts","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(or (not offers_gift) all_gifts_are_fee_discounts)","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor has_product_promotion_link)"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Does the full Code provision confirm the broader product scope?","Does authoritative guidance support the assumed component-by-component treatment of mixed offers?"],"statement":"For the circular’s defined distributors, read u14 as a gift control covering promotion of any specific investment product or product type. The fee-or-charge discount exception remains available when the gift is linked to a product type. Neither absence of structured-product status nor section 103 authorization independently excuses a non-discount gift under this selected control.","subject":"Selected paragraph-10 gift-promotion control: broad product scope with retained discount exception"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.84e49f3d524cb308835f7db4","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0}],"pending":null,"provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1","retrievals":[{"missing_dependencies":["external-authorities.23ec46"],"node_id":"node.84e49f3d524cb308835f7db4","retained_uncited_units":[{"locator":"Retained text line 2","normative":true,"span":{"end":507,"id":"s.u2","page":1,"quote_sha256":"ea2b8a878841df5955c78edc6cae47446483b86e3f5ccb04e1a8d940cf7e59fd","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":497,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Background","unit_id":"u2"},{"locator":"Retained text line 3","normative":true,"span":{"end":787,"id":"s.u3","page":1,"quote_sha256":"1af11939ea26428b3ebc908947bc9c1f16f0e153b769d724370e402bef46d880","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":512,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"In some cases, distributors promoted SFC-authorised funds (often via online platforms) and offered or imposed additional or distinct features or restrictions (eg, “guaranteed returns” or “lock-up periods”) beyond the product features set out in the funds’ offering documents.","unit_id":"u3"},{"locator":"Retained text line 4","normative":true,"span":{"end":1110,"id":"s.u4","page":1,"quote_sha256":"bb5d6d0066f0f3d1f31abecdaf338ffa59419754230c95ee338e84e9f9bf3161","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":792,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"In other cases, distributors asked clients to provide a mandate or standing instruction to invest in one or more SFC-authorised funds under specific circumstances, eg, using idle money in a client’s securities trading account with an aim to generate additional returns, albeit without any guaranteed or specific rates.","unit_id":"u4"},{"locator":"Retained text line 5","normative":true,"span":{"end":1265,"id":"s.u5","page":1,"quote_sha256":"8f21351a0ccdff701f2cc91871495aa1a1f6c2eb489975ea56821f8b71361cda","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":1115,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"These SFC-authorised funds and services were often promoted by the distributors to the public through aggressive and high-profile marketing campaigns.","unit_id":"u5"},{"locator":"Retained text line 6","normative":true,"span":{"end":1285,"id":"s.u6","page":1,"quote_sha256":"3502a56f7cfc1882bcea56240e2049ac086a6dd493f2f798572984a462255832","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":1267,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Guaranteed returns","unit_id":"u6"},{"locator":"Retained text line 7","normative":true,"span":{"end":1355,"id":"s.u7","page":1,"quote_sha256":"03c2ce4fec643340916926d6501ab8c112939a4757a21957ef88cb03e5d60fdb","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":1287,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Section 103 of the Securities and Futures Ordinance (Cap. 571) (SFO)","unit_id":"u7"},{"locator":"Retained text line 8","normative":true,"span":{"end":1646,"id":"s.u8","page":1,"quote_sha256":"94608f831bfe0bc9746af9dc0219689b16aafe90a74711539afe5f3d6f65302e","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":1360,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Typically, the “guaranteed returns” in such cases comprise: (i) the actual return of the relevant fund(s) invested by the investor (ie, fund return); and (ii) a top-up return to make up the difference between the fund return and the guaranteed rate of return offered by the distributor.","unit_id":"u8"},{"locator":"Retained text line 9","normative":true,"span":{"end":1935,"id":"s.u9","page":1,"quote_sha256":"c775d212de8b31011848e316ed775c7903d2a3439d14f1d0b43c68812f8f7fc6","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":1651,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"The SFC wishes to remind intermediaries who engage in promotional activities that these guaranteed return arrangements may constitute a \"structured product\" under the SFO if the return to investors is determined by reference to the change in value of any securities (including funds).","unit_id":"u9"},{"locator":"Retained text line 10","normative":true,"span":{"end":2234,"id":"s.u10","page":1,"quote_sha256":"da3d5056c84f1786f1d7407d2638edfe2d9c59c7c2bfab11e30f99901b252a22","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":1940,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"It is an offence under section 103 of the SFO for a person to issue an advertisement, invitation or document which is or contains an invitation to the Hong Kong public to enter into or offer to enter into any structured products, unless the SFC has authorised the issue or an exemption applies.","unit_id":"u10"},{"locator":"Retained text line 11","normative":true,"span":{"end":2601,"id":"s.u11","page":1,"quote_sha256":"b226a3d2cbdb1fed01e7c813e12644c991178112e7df12c5b5b06ada5cd3ff7e","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":2239,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"SFC-authorised funds without guaranteed features are required to highlight in their offering documents that they do not have these features and that investors may not get back the principal of their investment1. As such, any guaranteed returns provided by distributors may create a misleading impression that these returns are provided by the underlying fund(s).","unit_id":"u11"},{"locator":"Retained text line 12","normative":true,"span":{"end":2641,"id":"s.u12","page":1,"quote_sha256":"195534ad5daed52e7ac87063b4aecc79dc0bb389cebc88cc9215bac090ef2f22","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":2603,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct2","unit_id":"u12"},{"locator":"Retained text line 15","normative":true,"span":{"end":4020,"id":"s.u15","page":1,"quote_sha256":"0fcee085b229ca8050a6fb6fdbc96da2f7a4dd33363295ece373b0fe323a3f89","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":3675,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"In light of the concerns set out from paragraphs 5 to 10 above, when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns (which are not part of the product features set out in the relevant offering documents) or other incentives to investors in breach of section 103 of the SFO or paragraph 3.11 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"u15"},{"locator":"Retained text line 16","normative":true,"span":{"end":4058,"id":"s.u16","page":1,"quote_sha256":"dda918bbe82f30ddab28135039fbc339acf16acc07deb67f6babf9b2b2757743","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":4022,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Lock-up period and dealing frequency","unit_id":"u16"},{"locator":"Retained text line 17","normative":true,"span":{"end":4354,"id":"s.u17","page":1,"quote_sha256":"2f891b58037e676dcd695c3baf69a86f4853ed05e667c205c42107b8af4b853f","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":4063,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"When distributing SFC-authorised funds, some distributors imposed a lock-up period on their clients’ investments or lowered the funds’ dealing frequency. For instance, clients’ redemption was only allowed on a weekly or monthly basis even though the fund provided daily dealing arrangements.","unit_id":"u17"},{"locator":"Retained text line 18","normative":true,"span":{"end":4874,"id":"s.u18","page":1,"quote_sha256":"08297ac978b8b5eaf5dfc9048caf8c3b306c0cb224d151e2108633ea28bb7597","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":4359,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Distributors should act fairly and in the best interests of their clients in providing services in accordance with General Principle 1 (Honesty and fairness) of the Code of Conduct. They should not restrict a client’s right to redeem his or her investment in a fund pursuant to the dealing frequency specified in the fund’s offering documents. Such restrictions would limit the client’s ability to make effective and timely investment decisions in response to changing market conditions or individual circumstances.","unit_id":"u18"},{"locator":"Retained text line 19","normative":true,"span":{"end":5228,"id":"s.u19","page":1,"quote_sha256":"3d8087781b49ce535e15631e7265887d0afb4fbe07c78026ba6deb62cf847c20","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":4879,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"While distributors of SFC-authorised funds may have different fund dealing procedures or cut-off times for administrative efficiency, the SFC expects them to use their best endeavours to adhere to a fund’s dealing frequency as stipulated in its offering documents when dealing in the fund for clients, and not to reduce the fund’s dealing frequency.","unit_id":"u19"},{"locator":"Retained text line 20","normative":true,"span":{"end":5252,"id":"s.u20","page":1,"quote_sha256":"7e1dfa66af384d4b087a94fecfb2cecfa563dd744d656ea862ae5f640932f566","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":5230,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Other marketing issues","unit_id":"u20"},{"locator":"Retained text line 21","normative":true,"span":{"end":5898,"id":"s.u21","page":1,"quote_sha256":"994420732f7ffb764258e7b4c4c102643e363748d0214053741f033cbfb141eb","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":5257,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"In some cases, distributors offered or marketed the services described in paragraph 3 above without any guaranteed rates of return, but highlighted the regular interest payments or distribution features of the services prominently (eg, interest generated daily, or clients’ potential financial return from using such services), which would in fact be derived from the actual return(s) of the underlying fund(s). In preparing invitations and advertisements to promote their services, intermediaries should ensure that they do not contain any misleading or deceptive information, and they must comply with paragraph 2.3 of the Code of Conduct.","unit_id":"u21"},{"locator":"Retained text line 22","normative":true,"span":{"end":6369,"id":"s.u22","page":1,"quote_sha256":"bc704754c5b7c9c59e6a6b494dd6f9505f930ae4b36a37aa02d6368c69a4edf2","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":5903,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Where a distributor highlights in an advertisement the financial return of its services, which is in fact derived from the actual return(s) of the underlying SFC-authorised fund(s), the advertisement, particularly the presentation of financial return relating to the services, should be prepared in a manner that is consistent with the principles under the SFC’s Advertising Guidelines Applicable to Collective Investment Schemes Authorized under the Product Codes4.","unit_id":"u22"},{"locator":"Retained text line 23","normative":true,"span":{"end":7002,"id":"s.u23","page":1,"quote_sha256":"20ecbac168ce1f7902c8b60784189a57017881fb8408fea1d9d3bd707bea3b74","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":6374,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Specifically, the advertisements of these services should avoid giving a misleading impression that the relevant services or underlying fund(s) would generate positive or guaranteed returns without any risk of loss. In addition, the advertisements should not draw a parallel between the services and the placement of cash on deposits, imply they are deposit-like arrangements (including any comparisons between the financial returns of the services and bank deposit rates), or suggest that the services are, or are equivalent to, bank deposits or savings (eg, by emphasising the services can address investors’ “savings needs”).","unit_id":"u23"},{"locator":"Retained text line 24","normative":true,"span":{"end":7178,"id":"s.u24","page":1,"quote_sha256":"b9db4855c8d4944ebdfe0009a08ee4d1623c21e673c1c221a04b1bab3f6497ec","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":7007,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"The SFC will closely monitor market practices concerning the promotion of SFC-authorised funds and may take regulatory action and issue further guidance where appropriate.","unit_id":"u24"},{"locator":"Retained text line 25","normative":true,"span":{"end":7274,"id":"s.u25","page":1,"quote_sha256":"0e3225addfcc2663ed547268443c0eda4c4b22cc50e1f858008119256b3a532c","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":7186,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Intermediaries Supervision Department                       Investment Products Division","unit_id":"u25"},{"locator":"Retained text line 26","normative":true,"span":{"end":7392,"id":"s.u26","page":1,"quote_sha256":"65ef453c883837716ab8837d02d9559715cd243baf93ca1a5cf70be2d67b8492","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":7275,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Intermediaries Division                                                             Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"u26"},{"locator":"Retained text line 27","normative":true,"span":{"end":7426,"id":"s.u27","page":1,"quote_sha256":"88e2bc94e9edc39f2ac1cdaaea86b44ab5ea59b31c446f69591f21bf460b005e","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":7393,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"u27"},{"locator":"Retained text line 28","normative":true,"span":{"end":7985,"id":"s.u28","page":1,"quote_sha256":"bf5f8b77f3976a352737ec8fbcfd51cec4ddf8c7ebfa8bcec39b200cf36f6a6c","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":7511,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"1 Pursuant to 6.4 of the Overarching Principles Section as set out in the SFC Handbook for Unit Trusts and Mutual Funds, Investment-Linked Assurance Schemes and Unlisted Structured Investment Products, offering documents of an SFC-authorised fund shall contain the information necessary for investors to be able to make an informed judgement of the investment whilst all key features and risks of the fund shall be highlighted prominently in a succinct manner for investors.","unit_id":"u28"},{"locator":"Retained text line 29","normative":true,"span":{"end":8108,"id":"s.u29","page":1,"quote_sha256":"4c6f6c26a269f1395844e4e68ad8b7b0dc9a752bf58521543258b9ca6360144b","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":7987,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"2 The Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"u29"},{"locator":"Retained text line 30","normative":true,"span":{"end":8233,"id":"s.u30","page":1,"quote_sha256":"7d1b57b24a3d3a602b7413d75e6e6c8469cf4f2366245996989f8837b9944ce3","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":8110,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"3 The answer to question 1 of the frequently asked questions on the Code of Conduct issued by the SFC on 30 September 2010.","unit_id":"u30"},{"locator":"Retained text line 31","normative":true,"span":{"end":8342,"id":"s.u31","page":1,"quote_sha256":"7d11e9adab289c660270ea1d9d1de8ece380656044c134d8dcd9eaaedd938b50","raw_sha256":"517ea55a89069338cde4b0ed0d75226e09967afc47c47de14c31303a5f430df9","source_id":"23EC46","start":8235,"text_sha256":"a1bb2e92c24fd0dce2e6fc73aa164bc7455ca672504a1ee86c180e9457f97f9e"},"text":"4 As supplemented by the frequently asked questions and other guidance issued by the SFC from time to time.","unit_id":"u31"}]}],"rounds":1,"roundtrips":[],"run_id":"run.43cfe1f6c26f47b89fa28eb53ba97027","stop":null}